Provenance of adapted files
===========================

Part of this composer is adapted from drm-hwcomposer rather than written
here. Those files keep their original copyright headers, and this file
records where each of them came from, so that a later reader can diff
against the original and see exactly what was changed and why.

Upstream:   https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/drm-hwcomposer/drm-hwcomposer
Base:       da06409105fe03cc0f2f2090f88af96fd0e5053e
            with 5b36732 ("Remove hwc2_device") reverted

Why that base. The HWC2 entry point was removed upstream on 2025-12-11,
and the layer-mapping work landed after it, so neither point of the
history has both. Reverting the removal onto the current tree brings the
two together: the revert applies without a conflict, and of the thirty
two members the entry point reaches for on the display, three no longer
exist -- each with a direct successor.

What is left out. Everything that speaks to the display through DRM/KMS:
this kernel has no DRM driver for the display controller at all, and the
hardware is driven through tegra_dc_ext instead. Also left out are the
parts with no counterpart on this board: HDCP, flattening telemetry, and
the vendor backends for other hardware.


Adapted files
-------------

Taken unchanged unless a note says otherwise. Paths are the same on both
sides.

  utils/fd.h
  utils/fd.cpp
  utils/log.h
  compositor/DisplayInfo.h
  compositor/FrameTimeHistory.h
  compositor/FrameTimeHistory.cpp
  compositor/LayerData.h
  bufferinfo/BufferInfo.h
  bufferinfo/BufferInfoGetter.h
  bufferinfo/BufferInfoGetter.cpp
  display/PipelineBinding.h
      From drm/DrmDisplayPipeline.h, the two templates that say who a piece
      of display hardware currently belongs to. They are here because they
      know nothing about DRM, while the rest of that file is nothing else.
      Changed: the thing bound to is a pipeline as this composer describes
      one.

  bufferinfo/GrallocBufferHandle.h
  bufferinfo/GrallocBufferHandle.cpp
      Changed: the handle is kept rather than imported. The mapper on this
      platform wants a full description of the buffer alongside the handle,
      which this function is not given; and the import is not needed here,
      because the handle arrives over the interface into the process this
      runs in and what reaches the display is one of its own descriptors.

  display/DrmMode.h
  display/DrmMode.cpp
      From drm/DrmMode.{h,cpp}.
      Changed: CreateModeBlob is not here. It registers a timing as a
      property object on a DRM device, and there is no such device on this
      board -- nothing to register against and nothing that would read it.
      Standing something in for it would mean writing a mock of an interface
      this hardware does not have, which is worse than the absence: the
      absence is true. Everything else in the file is unchanged.

  backend/BackendDisplayCapabilities.h
      Changed twice, both because of the platform rather than the board.
      The list of high-dynamic-range types is named through a package this
      release predates, so it is named the way the rest of upstream names it
      -- ui::Hdr, which this release does have. And a guard was added: the
      file has none upstream, where it is included from exactly one place.

  compositor/FlatteningController.cpp
      Changed: one added include. The lock-assertion helper it uses arrived
      in the platform's thread annotations after this release; every macro
      it is written in terms of is here, so the class is declared where the
      platform would declare it, in utils/ThreadAnnotations.h.

  compositor/LayerToPlaneJoiningPlan.h
      Changed: the pipeline is forward-declared as a struct, which is what
      it is. Upstream says class and its own build only warns.
